---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { IMG } from '../images';
const path = '/it-asset-recycling';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'IT Asset Recycling', href: path }];
const equipment = [
  'Laptops / notebooks', 'Desktop computers', 'Apple products (Mac, iPad, iPhone)', 'Mobile phones and tablets',
  'Monitors and peripherals', 'Servers and racks', 'Network switches and equipment', 'Printers', 'Copiers', 'Scanners',
  'Cameras', 'Audio-visual equipment', 'Teleconferencing and IP telephony equipment', 'Cabling', 'UPS and power supplies',
];
---
<Base
  title="IT Asset Disposal & E-Waste Recycling with Secure Data Sanitization"
  description="Secure IT asset disposal and e-waste recycling for organizations in Singapore: ISO 9001 & 14001 certified, NIST 800-88 erasure, next-business-day collection."
  path={path}
  crumbs={crumbs}
  image={IMG.circuitBoards.src}
>
  <PageHero
    crumbs={crumbs}
    eyebrow="IT asset disposal"
    title="IT Asset Disposal and Recycling"
    lead="Organization IT asset and e-waste recycling, made safe through secure data sanitization."
  >
    <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn--accent" href="/contact-us#quote">Book a collection</a></div>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="stack">
        <h2>IT asset and e-waste disposal and recycling for organizations</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>ISO 9001 and 14001 certified processes for data destruction and disposal of IT equipment and e-waste</li>
          <li>US NIST 800-88 Rev 1 compliant <a href="/data-sanitization">erasure</a> of all data storage media and information</li>
          <li>One-stop solution for businesses and organizations, with next-business-day* collection</li>
          <li>Used by many organizations, including MNCs, schools, hospitals and cyber security firms</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Dispose of or recycle your IT assets securely and responsibly. <a href="/contact-us">Contact us today</a>, or find out more about <a href="/about-us">why Databyte Solution</a>.</p>
        <p class="small muted">*Please confirm collection timing with us when booking.</p>
      </div>
      <Photo img={IMG.equipmentTypes} alt="Types of IT equipment we handle: computers, drives, circuit boards and components" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--light">
    <div class="wrap stack-lg">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>E-waste and equipment we handle</h2>
        <p class="lead">Databyte Solution handles a wide range of IT equipment, including:</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="checklist cols-2">
        {equipment.map((e) => <li>{e}</li>)}
        <li>Other equipment and e-waste: <a href="/contact-us">please ask us</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="wrap stack-lg">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Reduce, Reuse, Recycle</span>
        <h2>The 3Rs, in order</h2>
        <p class="lead">Reduce, Reuse, Recycle are terms we often hear. Did you know they are in order of priority?</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card"><h3>1. Reduce</h3><p><strong>Use only what you need and reduce waste.</strong></p><p class="muted">Organizations can extend the life of assets and equipment where possible, reducing the waste generated.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>2. Reuse</h3><p><strong>Use things again, for the same or a new purpose.</strong></p><p class="muted">Working parts such as RAM, LCDs, keyboards and power supplies can be recovered to repair and refurbish other devices.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>3. Recycle</h3><p><strong>Turn waste into useful products.</strong></p><p class="muted">Circuit boards and metals are processed to extract resources, instead of mining them from the ground.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p>Following the 3Rs protects the environment, conserves limited resources, reduces the space needed for waste disposal facilities and extends the lifespan of landfills.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--light">
    <div class="wrap split split--top">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">What needs to be sanitized during recycling?</h2>
        <p>
          Storage media includes solid state drives, hard disk drives and other storage types. These need to be evaluated and
          categorized to set the level of sanitization required (<a href="/data-sanitization/clear-purge-destroy">Clear, Purge or Destroy</a>),
          according to the organization's data classification.
        </p>
        <p>
          For information with a high security categorization, storage media should be destroyed. For lower classifications, NIST SP
          800-88 Rev 1 allows media to be cleared or purged, documented, and then recycled instead of destroyed.
        </p>
        <p>
          More on security categorization: <a href="https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/Legacy/SP/nistspecialpublication800-60v1r1.pdf" rel="noopener">NIST SP 800-60 Rev 1</a>.
          <a href="https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/FIPS/NIST.FIPS.199.pdf" rel="noopener">FIPS 199</a> sets security categories based
          on the magnitude of harm expected from a compromise, and organizations can use it as a general principle.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="figure">
        <Photo img={IMG.nistFlow} alt="NIST 800-88 flowchart for choosing Clear, Purge or Destroy by security categorization" />
        <figcaption>Sanitization and disposition decision flow, NIST SP 800-88 Rev 1.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="wrap stack-lg">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Our e-waste sorting and recycling process</h2>
        <p class="lead">Every item that arrives at Databyte Solution is sorted to maximize reuse and recycling.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><strong>Equipment type</strong><span>Sorted into categories such as network equipment, cables, desktop computers and monitors.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Condition</strong><span>Working equipment is set aside for reuse; working parts are stripped from non-working equipment as spares (reduce).</span></li>
        <li><strong>Material type</strong><span>Hazardous materials such as batteries and toner are removed. Metals and circuit boards go to material recycling (recycle).</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        This process maximizes what is reused and reduces the waste generated. Parts and materials that cannot be reused efficiently
        are disassembled and sent to dedicated facilities for material extraction and recycling. Only materials that cannot be
        recycled are sent for incineration and landfill.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid--4">
        <article class="card card--flush"><Photo img={IMG.circuitBoards} alt="Pile of circuit boards" class="card-media" /><div class="card-body"><h3>Circuit boards</h3><p class="muted small">Metals and materials extracted for recycling.</p></div></article>
        <article class="card card--flush"><Photo img={IMG.hddsForRecycling} alt="Hard disk drives sorted for recycling" class="card-media" /><div class="card-body"><h3>Hard disk drives</h3><p class="muted small">Magnetic materials and metals extracted for processing and reuse.</p></div></article>
        <article class="card card--flush"><Photo img={IMG.heatSinks} alt="CPU heat sinks" class="card-media" /><div class="card-body"><h3>CPU heat sinks</h3><p class="muted small">Metal recycling.</p></div></article>
        <article class="card card--flush"><Photo img={IMG.cables} alt="Tangled cables and connectors" class="card-media" /><div class="card-body"><h3>Cables and connectors</h3><p class="muted small">Conductive metal (e.g. copper) recycling.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--light">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">What should be reused and recycled?</h2>
      <p>
        Machines, equipment and parts with no built-in memory or information storage can and should be repurposed or reused. This
        includes laptop, desktop, server and networking hardware once storage media such as hard disks, SSDs and flash memory cards
        are removed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some storage cannot be removed, such as storage chips soldered onto certain Apple machines and other manufacturers' newer
        devices. Depending on the sensitivity of the data, the choice is then to securely erase and purge the data on the machine, or
        to destroy the device's circuit board by shredding.
      </p>
      <p>
        For these devices, we reuse and recycle as many parts as possible that are certain not to contain any information, such as
        LCDs, keyboards and chassis. They are used to repair and refurbish other devices, extending their life before they enter the
        waste stream.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand title="Clearing out old IT equipment?" text="Tell us what you have. We collect, sanitize, and reuse or recycle it responsibly." />
</Base>
